    <li>Bryan, Michael F., Stephen G. Cecchetti, and Rodney L. Wiggins II, &ldquo;Efficient Inflation Estimation,&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland, Working Paper No. 97-07, August 1997. (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://fraser.stlouisfed.org/title/working-paper-federal-reserve-bank-cleveland-4494/efficient-inflation-estimation-552579" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-wp-199707</a>)</li>
    <li>Campos, Chris, Michael McMain, and Mathieu Pedemonte, &ldquo;Understanding Which Prices Affect Inflation Expectations,&rdquo; Economic Commentary, Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland, Number 2022-06, April 19, 2022. (<a href="https://www.clevelandfed.org/publications/economic-commentary/2022/ec-202206-understanding-which-prices-affect-inflation-expectations">https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-ec-202206</a>)</li>
    <li>Candia, Bernardo, Olivier Coibion, and Yuriy Gorodnichenko, &ldquo;The Inflation Expectations of U.S. Firms: Evidence from a New Survey,&rdquo; National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 28836, May 2021. (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.nber.org/papers/w28836" target="_blank">http://www.nber.org/papers/w28836</a>)</li>
    <li>Cavallo, Alberto, Guillermo Cruces, and Ricardo Perez-Truglia, &ldquo;Inflation Expectations, Learning, and Supermarket Prices: Evidence from Survey Experiments,&rdquo; American Economic Journal: Macroeconomics 9, 2017, pp. 1-35. (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.aeaweb.org/articles?id=10.1257/mac.20150147" target="_blank">https://www.aeaweb.org/articles?id=10.1257/mac.20150147</a>)</li>
    <li>Coibion, Olivier, and Yuriy Gorodnichenko, &ldquo;Is the Phillips Curve Alive and Well after All? Inflation Expectations and the Missing Disinflation,&rdquo; American Economic Journal: Macroeconomics 7, 2015, pp. 197-232. (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://dx.doi.org/10.1257/mac.20130306" target="_blank">http://dx.doi.org/10.1257/mac.20130306</a>)</li>
    <li>Crone, Theodore M., N. Neil K. Khettry, Loretta J. Mester, and Jason A. Novak, &ldquo;Core Measures of Inflation as Predictors of Total Inflation,&rdquo; Journal of Money, Credit and Banking 45 (March-April 2013), pp. 505-519. (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://doi.org/10.1111/jmcb.12013" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.1111/jmcb.12013</a>)</li>
    <li>D&rsquo;Acunto, Francesco, Ulrike Malmendier, Juan Ospina, and Michael Weber, &ldquo;Exposure to Grocery Prices and Inflation Expectations,&rdquo; Journal of Political Economy 129, 2021, pp 1615-1639. (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://doi.org/10.1086/713192" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.1086/713192</a>)</li>
    <li>Dietrich, Alexander M., Edward S. Knotek II, Kristian Ove R. Myrseth, Robert W. Rich, Raphael S. Schoenle, and Michael Weber. &ldquo;Greater Than the Sum of the Parts: Aggregate vs. Aggregated Inflation Expectations,&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland, Working Paper No. 22-20, June 2022. (<a href="https://www.clevelandfed.org/publications/working-paper/2022/wp-2220-greater-than-the-sum-of-the-parts-aggregate-vs-aggregated-inflation-expectations">https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-wp-202220</a>)</li>
    <li>Dogra, Keshav, Sebastian Heise, Edward S. Knotek II, Brent Meyer, Robert W. Rich, Raphael S. Schoenle, Giorgio Topa, Wilbert van der Klaauw, and W&auml;ndi Bruine de Bruin, &ldquo;Estimates of Cost-Price Passthrough from Business Survey Data.&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland, Working Paper No. 23-14, June 2023. (<a href="https://www.clevelandfed.org/publications/working-paper/2023/wp-2314-estimates-of-cost-price-passthrough-from-business-survey-data">https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-wp-202314</a>)</li>
    <li>Federal Open Market Committee, &ldquo;Statement on Longer-Run Goals and Monetary Policy Strategy,&rdquo; reaffirmed effective January 31, 2023. (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/files/FOMC_LongerRunGoals.pdf" target="_blank">https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/files/FOMC_LongerRunGoals.pdf</a>)</li>
